From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:44:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 016/117] power: supply: bq27xxx: return cycle count read
 errors

bq27xxx_battery_read_cyct() logged a failed register read but still
returned success and exposed the negative errno as a cycle count.

Return the transport error immediately so callers can distinguish
unavailable data from a valid count. Successful reads and transport
behavior are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: 466688c2cdaf04d0d06efddbb0f7f1d7df9c4442
---
 drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
index 01c9ec111..6c907b66b 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1739,8 +1739,10 @@ static int bq27xxx_battery_read_cyct(struct bq27xxx_device_info *di,
 	int cyct;
 
 	cyct = bq27xxx_read(di, BQ27XXX_REG_CYCT, false);
-	if (cyct < 0)
+	if (cyct < 0) {
 		dev_err(di->dev, "error reading cycle count total\n");
+		return cyct;
+	}
 
 	val->intval = cyct;
 
